---
import StaticPage from '../layouts/StaticPage.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
---

<StaticPage
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="How Baggage Gear collects, uses and protects information when you visit the site, including cookies, analytics, ads and affiliate links."
	icon="lock"
	lead="Short version: I collect very little, I don’t sell your personal information, and you can ask me about your data at any time."
	c1="#1b2447"
	c2="#4c5fb0"
	updated="October 8, 2026"
>
	<ul class="glance">
		<li style="--c1:#1b2447;--c2:#4c5fb0">
			<span class="chip sm"><Icon name="database" size={18} /></span>
			<strong>What I collect</strong>
			Basic visit data through cookies and analytics, plus anything you choose to email me.
		</li>
		<li style="--c1:#0b5f59;--c2:#1fb5a6">
			<span class="chip sm"><Icon name="ban" size={18} /></span>
			<strong>What I don’t do</strong>
			I don’t sell or rent your personal information to anyone.
		</li>
		<li style="--c1:#9a4a07;--c2:#f0a02a">
			<span class="chip sm"><Icon name="cookie" size={18} /></span>
			<strong>Your choices</strong>
			Manage cookies in your browser, and ask me to access, fix or delete your data.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<p>
		At <strong>Baggage Gear</strong>, your privacy matters. This policy explains what information the site
		collects, how it is used, and what choices you have. By using the site, you agree to the practices described
		here.
	</p>

	<h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
	<h3>Information you give me</h3>
	<p>
		If you email me through the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>, I receive your name, email address and
		whatever you write. I collect this <strong>only when you choose to send it</strong>.
	</p>
	<h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
	<p>When you visit, cookies, analytics tools and server logs may record:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Browser type and version, operating system and device type</li>
		<li>IP address and approximate location</li>
		<li>Pages visited, time on site and the page or search that referred you</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>2. How I use information</h2>
	<ol>
		<li><strong>Running the site:</strong> delivering articles and keeping pages working.</li>
		<li><strong>Improving content:</strong> seeing which guides are read and which are confusing.</li>
		<li><strong>Replying to you:</strong> answering questions and messages you send.</li>
		<li><strong>Affiliate tracking:</strong> crediting purchases made through affiliate links (see the <a href="/disclosure/">Disclosure</a>).</li>
		<li><strong>Legal compliance:</strong> meeting legal obligations and protecting the site.</li>
	</ol>
	<div class="callout">
		<span class="chip sm"><Icon name="shield" size={18} /></span>
		<div><strong>I do not sell or rent your personal information</strong> to third parties.</div>
	</div>

	<h2>3. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
	<p>Baggage Gear may use these kinds of cookies:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Essential:</strong> remember basics such as your light or dark theme.</li>
		<li><strong>Performance:</strong> show how visitors use the site so it can be improved.</li>
		<li><strong>Advertising and affiliate:</strong> show relevant ads and track affiliate referrals through partner services.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Where required, a consent banner lets you choose which cookies to allow. You can also block or delete cookies in
		your browser settings, although some features may then work less well.
	</p>

	<h2>4. Third-party services</h2>
	<p>The site may rely on outside providers, including:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Affiliate programs</strong> such as Amazon Associates</li>
		<li><strong>Advertising partners</strong> such as Google AdSense</li>
		<li><strong>Analytics tools</strong> such as Google Analytics</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		These providers have their own privacy policies and practices, which I don’t control. I encourage you to read
		them.
	</p>

	<h2>5. Email</h2>
	<p>
		I use your email address to reply to you. If I ever send newsletters or updates, you’ll be able to unsubscribe
		at any time, and I’ll remove you promptly when you ask.
	</p>

	<h2>6. Data security</h2>
	<p>
		I take reasonable steps to protect information, including serving the site over a secure connection and
		limiting what I collect in the first place. No website can promise perfect security, so I can’t guarantee it.
	</p>

	<h2>7. Children’s privacy</h2>
	<p>
		Baggage Gear is <strong>not directed to children under 13</strong>, and I don’t knowingly collect their
		personal information. If you believe a child has sent me personal data, <a href="/contact/">contact me</a>
		and I’ll delete it.
	</p>

	<h2>8. Links to other sites</h2>
	<p>
		Articles link to airlines, stores and other sites. I’m not responsible for their privacy practices, so please
		review their policies when you leave Baggage Gear.
	</p>

	<h2>9. Your rights</h2>
	<p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to:</p>
	<ul class="ticks">
		<li>Access the personal information I hold about you</li>
		<li>Ask me to correct or delete it</li>
		<li>Opt out of marketing messages</li>
		<li>Opt out of certain cookie-based advertising</li>
	</ul>
	<p>To make a request, <a href="/contact/">contact me</a> and describe what you need.</p>

	<h2>10. Legal disclosure</h2>
	<p>
		I may disclose information if the law requires it, to protect the safety or rights of the site and its
		visitors, or to investigate fraud and violations of the <a href="/terms/">Terms</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
	<p>
		I may update this policy from time to time. Changes appear here with a new “Last updated” date, and continued
		use of the site means you accept the updated policy.
	</p>

	<h2>12. Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Questions or requests about privacy? Use the <a href="/contact/"><strong>Contact page</strong></a> or email
		<a href="mailto:iverjcalloway@gmail.com">iverjcalloway@gmail.com</a>.
	</p>
</StaticPage>
